course: dictionary
lesson: 3242
title: Envy: a feeling, a verb, a phrase
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Envy is the unhappy feeling you get when you want something someone else has, like their toys, skills or luck. «Feeling envy is normal; acting on it to hurt someone is the wrong part.» Everyone feels it sometimes. Notice it, but do not let it make you unkind.
explain: As a verb, envy is a doing word. «I envy your holiday!» means I wish I had your holiday. The verb changes: envies, envied, envying. «I don't envy you» means I would not like to be in your place, so it is not about wishing for something.
explain: Some phrases use envy too. «Green with envy» means feeling very jealous. Someone who is «the envy of the class» is admired and wanted by others. «Envy whispers that someone else's good thing is taken from you.» Envy is quiet and sneaky, so watch out for it.
fact: Envy means the unhappy feeling of wanting what someone else has.
fact: To envy someone is to wish you had what they have.
fact: «Greed» is wanting more than your share; «envy» is being sore that someone else has something good.
fact: Envy can make you say mean things you do not really believe, like calling something ugly because you want it.
fact: «Envy» is one of the seven deadly sins in Christian teaching, and fairy tales like Snow White show how it can cause harm.
exercise: «Envy whispers that someone else's good thing is taken from you.» What does envy mean in this sentence? | A loud noise from far away | A happy feeling of sharing a treat | A kind word to a friend | *The unhappy feeling of wanting what someone else has
exercise: Jess says, «I envy your holiday!» What does Jess mean? | I want to stop your holiday | I have never been on holiday | *I wish I had a holiday like yours | I am sorry your holiday was bad
exercise: Which phrase means someone is admired and wanted by others? | *The envy of the class | Full of envy | Green with sadness | I don't envy you
test: Which part is wrong? «Feeling envy is normal; acting on it to hurt someone is the wrong part.» | *Acting on it to hurt someone | Being a child | Feeling normal | Feeling envy
test: Yesterday Sam ___ his friend's new bike. Which word fits? | Envy | *Envied | Envying | Envies
exam: Which is the best meaning of «I don't envy you»? | I am very jealous of you | I wish I had your place | I am proud of you | *I would not like to be in your place
